Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:31:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] Generator: verify-row cap, drafter/accept overlap,
 hybrid drafting for a single job

EXL3_DRAFT_MAX_ROWS=N caps a round's verify rows (jobs x (drafts + 1)) at N by trimming the draft width, so rounds
with 9-12 jobs stay inside the 64-row coop / graphed verify paths (no-op whenever jobs x (drafts + 1) <= N).
EXL3_SD_DRAFT_OVERLAP=1 (with EXL3_SD_BATCH_ACCEPT=1 and a DFlash drafter with sliding-window states): once the
round's samples are on the host, the predicted accepted lengths drive the drafter's K/V update and the next draft
block's launch before the host accept loop; the next round checks job set, positions and anchors and rolls the
block back on any mismatch (EOS, requeue, rewind, job start, prefill, checkpoint boundary, window shift).
EXL3_HYBRID_SOLO=1 runs hybrid (suffix-match) drafting only in rounds with exactly one active job.
The sampler past-ids fix of EXL3_SD_BATCH_ACCEPT also applies under EXL3_SD_BATCH_READBACK. All default off.
